      "message": "From review agent:\n\nThis logic appears to be inverted.\n\nIf `target-\u003econtents().type() !\u003d Value::NONE`, it is a target with explicit \u0027contents\u0027 which, according to the commit message and `NinjaGeneratedFileTargetWriter::Run()`, should be written immediately for performance.\n\nThe targets that perform metadata walks (and thus need to be delayed to avoid the race condition) are those where `target-\u003econtents().type() \u003d\u003d Value::NONE`.\n\nAs written, metadata-based files won\u0027t be recorded here and won\u0027t be written at the end of the build, while content-based files will be written twice (once in the target writer and once in the delayed callback).\n\n----\n\nAARGH, this is why this CL is faster, but it also means the problem is not completely fixed by it. If I correct the comparison here, we\u0027re back to 15%-20% slow down in `gn gen` time.\n\nWe\u0027re going to need to remove validations from metadata walks entirely after all. Damn, what a waste of time. Adding another -1 here.",
